# jobhunt workspace

Your private job-hunt folder: profile, CV, ratings, digests. Keep it private — it holds
personal data. Engine and full docs: https://github.com/jessefontaine/jobhunt

## Setup (once)

1. Edit `profile/profile.md` (and add rules to `profile/preferences.md` → `## Manual`).
2. Put your CV PDF in `docs/` and run `scripts/extract-cv.sh` (needs `pdftotext`), or write
   `docs/cv.md` by hand. The scorer reads `docs/cv.md`.
3. Edit `config/sources.yaml`: queries, and optionally `contact:`. `config/settings.yaml` (or
   the UI's Settings page) holds the rest: theme, score range, digest size, scoring model.
4. `claude login` once — scoring runs on your Claude subscription via the `claude` CLI.
5. `git init && git add -A && git commit -m "workspace"` (optional, recommended).

## Workflow

Easiest: `uv run jobhunt serve` opens a browser UI with buttons for everything below, a rating
queue, your shortlist, and editors for the profile files. Or from the terminal:

```bash
uv run jobhunt check   # fetch → score → write digests/<today>.md
```

Open the newest digest and fill in `rating:` (1–5) and optionally `note:` under listings, then:

```bash
uv run jobhunt rate    # ingest ratings, regenerate learned preferences after ≥3 new ratings
```

Rated listings leave the queue. The ones you rated 4–5 that are still open show up in a
`## Shortlist` at the top of each digest and in `shortlist.md` (`uv run jobhunt shortlist`
prints it). To change a rating, edit it in the digest you rated it in and run
`uv run jobhunt rate digests/<that-file>.md`.

| rating | meaning |
|--------|---------|
| 5 | apply |
| 4 | strong interest |
| 3 | maybe |
| 2 | not really |
| 1 | irrelevant |

Engine updates: the browser UI shows a banner with an *Update & restart* button when a newer
engine is on GitHub; from a terminal, `uv run jobhunt update`. If the banner never appears,
`uv run jobhunt update --check` says why — the dashboard's *What's new* panel says the same
thing, including the last error. `uv sync --upgrade-package jobhunt` always works as a
fallback.

Or open this folder in Claude Code and type `/jobhunt` — it runs the same commands, records
ratings you give in chat, talks through whether a role is worth applying to (it reads your
profile, preferences and CV), and turns a link you paste into a scored listing
(`uv run jobhunt add <url>`). If it inferred a preference you disagree with, say so: it writes
the correction into `## Manual` and regenerates the learned rules around it. `/jobhunt-sources`
adds a new site to watch. Other commands: `jobhunt fetch`, `jobhunt score`, `jobhunt digest`,
`jobhunt shortlist`, `jobhunt sources`, `jobhunt show <url>`, `jobhunt learn`,
`jobhunt calibration` (how well the scores match your ratings),
`jobhunt rate --rebuild`. After editing `profile/`, `uv run jobhunt check --rescore`
re-scores every listing that is still open (one Claude call per batch).
